THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION. UNDERAGE
DRINKING IS STRONGLY PROHIBITED.

00:01.167 --> 00:02.476
FORCEFUL ALCOHOL CONSUMPTION, BINGE
DRINKING, SHAMEFUL ACTS NOT ENCOURAGED.

00:02.477 --> 00:03.756
VIEW THIS AS A COMEDY. ALL CHARACTERS
APPEARING IN THIS WORK ARE OF LEGAL AGE.

00:03.757 --> 00:04.987
DUE TO RECENT COMPLIANCE ISSUES, THE
BLACK DOT SIZE HAS BEEN INCREASED BY 5%.

00:39.777 --> 00:44.277
IZU UNIVERSITY

00:47.787 --> 00:49.577
<i>Right now, we will begin...</i>

00:50.417 --> 00:54.478
<i>the examination on the crisis
of Shinichiro Yamamoto's virginity.</i>

01:06.177 --> 01:08.596
<i>Let's go take a trip
under the bright summer sun</i>

01:08.597 --> 01:11.846
GRAND BLUE DREAMING SEASON 3<i>To a city far away, what do you say?</i>

01:11.847 --> 01:14.226
<i>Let's go take a trip
under the bright summer sun</i>

01:14.227 --> 01:17.777
<i>To a city far away, what do you say?</i>

01:21.897 --> 01:23.736
<i>Wait a sec, another heatwave?</i>

01:23.737 --> 01:25.486
<i>Temperatures are rising... Huh?!</i>

01:25.487 --> 01:28.696
<i>Our original plans are
totally busted, what now?</i>

01:28.697 --> 01:31.496
<i>But honestly, I'm getting so hyped</i>

01:31.497 --> 01:34.166
<i>Alright, let's roll up
our sleeves and dive in</i>

01:34.167 --> 01:35.956
<i>Rub your sleepy eyes and jump up</i>

01:35.957 --> 01:37.376
<i>Grab the usual shades</i>

01:37.377 --> 01:40.296
<i>Check your gear: Iced coffee, thermos</i>

01:40.297 --> 01:42.966
<i>Clear blue skies, just a trick of summer</i>

01:42.967 --> 01:46.097
<i>The booming speakers
keep calling my name</i>

01:46.467 --> 01:48.967
<i>Even now, I still believe</i>

01:51.887 --> 01:53.846
<i>In unexpected encounters</i>

01:53.847 --> 01:56.396
<i>And the miracles of this season</i>

01:56.397 --> 01:59.686
<i>Summer brings
those swing swing emotions</i>

01:59.687 --> 02:02.436
<i>Ah, even if I get a little carried away</i>

02:02.437 --> 02:07.616
<i>On my mind,
I've only been searching for you</i>

02:07.617 --> 02:13.576
<i>Let the south wind blow you here,
just as you are</i>

02:13.577 --> 02:18.287
<i>Under the blue sky, hold me tight</i>

02:19.087 --> 02:24.193
<i>I want to dream
a summer dream with you</i>

02:26.877 --> 02:29.277
This is the assignment for today's class.

02:29.967 --> 02:31.542
GROUP DISCUSSION TOPIC:
SOLUTIONS FOR ISSUES AROUND US

02:31.543 --> 02:34.806
Each group will come up with a topic
and discuss it for 20 minutes.

02:34.807 --> 02:35.466
GROUP DISCUSSION TOPIC:
SOLUTIONS FOR ISSUES AROUND US

02:35.467 --> 02:37.496
TOPIC: SHINICHIROU YAMAMOTO'S
VIRGINITY ISSUE

02:37.497 --> 02:39.647
This is an extremely difficult problem.

02:39.857 --> 02:42.737
How are we men able to solve this?

02:42.987 --> 02:45.487
Are you guys making
a joke out of me?

02:45.777 --> 02:49.527
But if this discussion finds a solution...

02:50.377 --> 02:51.577
then you could...

02:51.887 --> 02:53.597
graduate from being a virgin!

02:53.807 --> 02:54.997
Gulp.

02:59.311 --> 03:00.562
The topic is settled.

03:00.905 --> 03:03.377
Then let's discuss the solution.

03:03.657 --> 03:04.547
Yeah, yeah.

03:04.707 --> 03:07.377
How do we help Yamamoto graduate
from his virginity?

03:07.867 --> 03:09.257
DISCARD, RECYCLE, GIVE OTHERS?
Hmm...

03:09.507 --> 03:10.506
SOLUTIONS: 1. USE MONEY

03:10.507 --> 03:12.387
2. USE FORCE TO COERCE
Only these two ways are logical.

03:12.687 --> 03:13.677
That's right.

03:13.937 --> 03:16.387
What about the option
of "getting a girlfriend"?

03:16.717 --> 03:19.267
3. USE DRUGS OR HYPNOSIS
Let's see, we have these three methods.

03:19.697 --> 03:22.517
That third option has way too many
unnecessary words attached.

03:23.197 --> 03:24.527
But hey, Kitahara,

03:24.657 --> 03:27.987
should we commit
a criminal offense as a solution?

03:28.217 --> 03:29.337
Agreed.

03:29.447 --> 03:30.907
That's too immoral.

03:31.287 --> 03:33.617
How can a nonexistent thingbe immoral?

03:34.177 --> 03:38.142
If so, this problem is
concluded as "inconclusive."

03:38.737 --> 03:39.737
Can't be helped.

03:40.007 --> 03:42.247
There is no solution to this.

03:42.577 --> 03:44.507
You bastards!

03:44.667 --> 03:47.167
Wait, it's too early to give up.

03:47.767 --> 03:50.717
Let's talk about the principles
of problem-solving first.

03:53.487 --> 03:57.477
When an issue arises that
we are unable to solve directly,

03:57.917 --> 04:02.017
there is still a way to change
the approach to achieve the goal.

04:03.547 --> 04:04.587
FLAT TIRE
For one example.

04:04.727 --> 04:07.397
If we're faced with the problem
of a "broken bicycle,"

04:07.507 --> 04:09.706
without any ability to fix it,

04:09.707 --> 04:10.276
IF YOU DON'T HAVE A BICYCLE,
JUST RUNNING THERE WILL DO

04:10.277 --> 04:11.948
we must rethink it as
"running there will do."

04:12.254 --> 04:13.378
IF YOU DON'T HAVE A BICYCLE, JUST RUNNING THERE WILL DO
IF YOU DON'T HAVE A BICYCLE, JUST RUNNING THERE WILL DO

04:13.379 --> 04:16.420
I see, so in short, what you mean is...

04:16.847 --> 04:20.666
does the partner to experience that with
necessarily have to be "human"?

04:20.667 --> 04:22.286
Yeah, exactly.

04:22.287 --> 04:24.587
Exactly my ass, you idiot!

04:25.117 --> 04:27.377
Stop messing around!

04:27.607 --> 04:29.587
Don't say that, Yamamoto.

04:29.937 --> 04:33.716
I think this is an opinion that is
scientific and highly logical.

04:33.717 --> 04:36.097
Huh? How is it logical?

04:36.427 --> 04:38.767
You're a science student,
so you should know this.

04:39.307 --> 04:41.596
It is the term "reading error."

04:41.597 --> 04:44.606
It's the error that occurs
when reading measured values below

04:44.607 --> 04:46.634
the smallest scale division using
an analog measuring instrument, right?

04:46.635 --> 04:49.356
4 HOURS 37 MINUTES
4 HOURS 38 MINUTES

04:49.357 --> 04:49.566
GROUP DISCUSSION TOPIC:
SOLUTIONS FOR ISSUES AROUND US

04:49.567 --> 04:51.061
This margin of error is normally
GROUP DISCUSSION TOPIC:

04:51.062 --> 04:51.906
SOLUTIONS FOR ISSUES AROUND US

04:51.907 --> 04:52.907
accepted at 10% of the
smallest scale division.

04:52.908 --> 04:54.246
GROUP DISCUSSION TOPIC:
SOLUTIONS FOR ISSUES AROUND US

04:54.247 --> 04:55.276
So what?

04:55.277 --> 04:55.745
GROUP DISCUSSION TOPIC:
SOLUTIONS FOR ISSUES AROUND US

04:55.746 --> 04:56.607
Furthermore,

04:57.317 --> 05:01.877
it is said that the genetic difference
between gorillas and humans is just 1%.

05:05.287 --> 05:07.636
Are you getting me to
"solve" it with a gorilla?

05:07.637 --> 05:10.796
And in the first place,
does he need to lose his virginity?

05:10.797 --> 05:11.837
Makes sense.

05:11.967 --> 05:15.717
Because the primitive purpose of
mating is to preserve the species.

05:16.107 --> 05:19.477
We need to reconsider whether he is
of value to humanity or not.

05:19.927 --> 05:23.097
I'm quietly listening and
you guys are shitting on me like that?

05:23.387 --> 05:26.016
Talking like that,
you must all have experience, yes?

05:26.017 --> 05:28.066
Very well, moving on to the next topic.

05:28.067 --> 05:29.686
Imamura, change the topic.

05:29.687 --> 05:30.237
Yeah.

05:30.407 --> 05:33.276
Unlike you guys,
I already have a target.

05:33.277 --> 05:35.316
<i>Do you want me to snap it or smash it?</i>

05:35.317 --> 05:36.406
What the hell?

05:36.407 --> 05:38.537
You haven't gotten anywhere with her!

05:38.787 --> 05:41.457
Just having a "target"
puts me above you guys.

05:43.037 --> 05:45.536
BURNING SOCIAL ISSUE: SOMEONE
LIKE KITAHARA HAVING A GIRLFRIEND

05:45.537 --> 05:47.557
PROPOSED BY
SHINICHIROU YAMAMOTO

05:47.757 --> 05:49.336
Then let's begin.

05:49.337 --> 05:49.797
Yeah.

05:50.207 --> 05:52.546
How should we resolve this?

05:52.547 --> 05:55.006
Making them break up
is the quickest way.

05:55.007 --> 05:57.197
But letting him live carefree
hurts the eye.

05:57.547 --> 05:59.806
DON'T DRAG ME INTO YOUR TOPIC!

05:59.807 --> 06:02.057
YOU STARTED IT!!

06:02.207 --> 06:05.346
As the one who proposed the topic,
I have a suggestion.

06:05.347 --> 06:05.977
Huh?

06:06.097 --> 06:08.767
I want to establish a rule
for this discussion.

06:08.907 --> 06:09.566
A rule?

06:09.567 --> 06:11.397
You mean a rule that we have to follow?

06:12.077 --> 06:12.777
That's right.

06:12.887 --> 06:15.776
Whatever conclusion is reached in
this discussion, I demand

06:15.777 --> 06:18.777
you guys must end it with the phrase
"Do XYZ then kill him."

06:19.007 --> 06:19.937
Approved.

06:20.247 --> 06:21.677
Exactly what I was thinking.

06:21.787 --> 06:24.417
If you hadn't said it,
I was going to propose it.

06:24.907 --> 06:27.287
Who was just talking big
about morals and stuff?

06:27.532 --> 06:28.876
So in my opinion...

06:28.877 --> 06:29.627
Wait a minute.

06:31.157 --> 06:32.657
I have another proposal.

06:32.917 --> 06:36.587
When you want to speak, you must raise
your hand to acquire permission.

06:36.807 --> 06:37.886
Permission?

06:37.887 --> 06:39.197
Why go that far?

06:39.847 --> 06:43.567
Because this discussion is also a trial.

06:44.027 --> 06:45.076
I see.

06:45.077 --> 06:47.336
This is a discussion about lives, after all.

06:47.337 --> 06:49.647
That logic is perfectly sound.

06:49.847 --> 06:52.646
Is there no premise
where you don't kill us?

06:52.647 --> 06:54.567
This resembles a witch hunt trial.

06:54.887 --> 06:55.977
Then, Chairman.

06:56.257 --> 06:57.067
Nojima.

06:57.267 --> 06:58.657
After I finish speaking,

06:58.837 --> 07:00.366
CEMENT
am I allowed to kill him?

07:00.367 --> 07:01.177
CEMENT
Granted.

07:01.497 --> 07:02.236
That easy?

07:02.237 --> 07:04.536
Our lives are being treated too cheaply!

07:04.537 --> 07:06.366
Whatever happens to this guy is fine.

07:06.367 --> 07:08.036
But at least please spare my life!

07:08.037 --> 07:09.666
No, spare my life!

07:09.667 --> 07:11.246
How shameful.

07:11.247 --> 07:13.507
As expected,
we should just off them both.

07:13.647 --> 07:16.586
I repeat, when you want to speak,
ask for permission first.

07:16.587 --> 07:17.626
Chairman.

07:17.627 --> 07:20.296
A permission to speak about
anything aside from mercy.

07:20.297 --> 07:21.577
Thank you very much.

07:22.027 --> 07:25.137
Although you are only targeting us,

07:25.797 --> 07:29.437
do you really think
we two are the only traitors here?

07:30.395 --> 07:31.177
<i>This damn Kitahara!</i>

07:31.297 --> 07:33.347
<i>What a terrifying statement.</i>

07:33.687 --> 07:36.946
Indeed, for someone as great as me
to not have a girlfriend is unnatural,

07:36.947 --> 07:38.657
or rather, having one is inevitable.

07:39.237 --> 07:41.907
Saying that much,
even the suspicion of betrayal is...

07:42.087 --> 07:43.906
There's no reason to suspect them.

07:43.907 --> 07:45.867
- Suspect us at least one bit, will you!
- Suspect us at least one bit, will you!

07:46.347 --> 07:48.117
Then what about Imamura?

07:48.277 --> 07:49.967
He's so handsome after all.

07:50.267 --> 07:52.627
Hmph, don't look down on me,
you lowly beings.

07:52.847 --> 07:55.586
My girlfriend lives in
a whole different world!

07:55.587 --> 07:56.417
Innocent.

07:57.007 --> 07:58.126
Damn it!

07:58.127 --> 08:00.007
What is this feeling of defeat?

08:00.307 --> 08:02.217
Well, we don't have much time left.

08:02.467 --> 08:05.306
First is the one whose attempt
has already been proven.

08:05.307 --> 08:06.927
Starting with Mitarai.

08:07.597 --> 08:11.437
Stop it!

08:13.577 --> 08:15.686
Next is Kitahara.

08:15.687 --> 08:17.276
Wait! Wait! Wait!

08:17.277 --> 08:18.856
I haven't done anything!

08:18.857 --> 08:23.617
I'm even facing
the same virginity issue as you, Yamamoto.

08:23.947 --> 08:24.657
Huh?

08:24.837 --> 08:26.156
IORI KITAHARA'S VIRGINITY CRISIS
Meaning if it's like this?

08:26.157 --> 08:27.577
IORI KITAHARA'S VIRGINITY CRISIS
It'll be no problem at all.

08:28.277 --> 08:29.786
So you guys shouldn't execute me...

08:29.787 --> 08:32.376
Well, time is almost up.

08:32.377 --> 08:35.587
Someone please give a statement
summarizing the chosen topic.

08:36.407 --> 08:36.846
Huh?

08:36.847 --> 08:38.337
IORI KITAHARA'S VIRGINITY CRISIS

08:38.647 --> 08:39.796
Excuse me.

08:39.797 --> 08:41.297
Allow me to change the topic...

08:42.287 --> 08:45.347
Please give your statement on that topic.

08:46.997 --> 08:48.118
Then, on behalf of the pack,

08:48.347 --> 08:52.047
regarding the constitutional crisis of
"Iori Kitahara's Virginity."...

08:52.207 --> 08:54.397
Those two still haven't done it?

08:54.827 --> 08:57.726
Kotegawa-san won't let him
get any action, will she?

08:57.727 --> 08:59.397
Good thing she's still pure.

08:59.607 --> 09:00.536
That idiot!

09:00.537 --> 09:02.237
Absolutely unforgivable!

09:03.367 --> 09:04.866
IORI KITAHARA'S VIRGINITY CRISIS
EXCELLENT

09:04.867 --> 09:06.026
SOMEHOW IT GOT A HIGH SCORE

09:06.027 --> 09:08.997
GRAND BLUE DREAMING SEASON 3

09:10.937 --> 09:13.126
No matter what you say, we won't remember.

09:13.127 --> 09:14.326
- That's right, that's right.
- You don't remember at all?

09:14.327 --> 09:15.536
We don't recall anything.

09:15.537 --> 09:18.626
<i>Third-year students like us
are almost all retiring.</i>

09:18.627 --> 09:20.126
No one remembers anything.

09:20.127 --> 09:22.427
<i>Is this the last summer
with all the seniors?</i>

09:23.107 --> 09:24.177
Hey, senpais.

09:25.457 --> 09:28.177
Is there anything you regret
not doing this summer?

09:28.447 --> 09:29.807
Regrets?

09:29.987 --> 09:31.726
Well, we have a few.

09:31.727 --> 09:33.227
Why ask out of the blue?

09:33.477 --> 09:34.877
Then let's just do them!

09:35.007 --> 09:37.457
This summer won't come back a second time.

09:40.547 --> 09:41.707
Iori.

09:42.667 --> 09:43.733
THINGS LEFT UNDONE THIS SUMMER
MEMORABLE DRINKING PARTY: I See...

09:44.000 --> 09:46.487
So it's wearing <i>yukata</i> and having
a drinking party with <i>takoyaki</i>, right?

09:46.592 --> 09:47.254
VERY IMPORTANT / LET'S GO ALL OUT WANT TO
MAKE TAKOYAKI: NICE! / I HAVE A MAKER / LET'S

09:47.255 --> 09:48.139
ADD VARIOUS STUFF EVERYONE IN YUKATA PROPERLY:
SO SUMMER-LIKE / GREAT / YOU GUYS HAVE IT?

09:48.140 --> 09:50.054
That sounds quite like a proper summer.

09:50.417 --> 09:52.657
Then it's decided
we'll wear <i>yukata</i> and gather.

09:53.237 --> 09:54.417
Nanaka, is that fine?

09:55.317 --> 09:57.227
Yeah, sure.

10:04.607 --> 10:07.427
What we need are just octopus
and <i>takoyaki</i> batter, right?

10:07.757 --> 10:09.807
That seems a bit too plain, doesn't it?

10:10.077 --> 10:13.557
We should also buy cheese,
sausages, or shrimp.

10:13.837 --> 10:14.837
Sounds great.

10:15.187 --> 10:17.727
Adding Kimchi and Mentaiko
would also be amazing.

10:17.887 --> 10:19.897
Just hearing it makes my mouth water.

10:20.357 --> 10:23.697
Or we could use hotcake batter
combined with chocolate.

10:24.287 --> 10:26.947
Is it okay to feed these guys sweets?

10:27.067 --> 10:28.367
I actually prefer that.

10:29.787 --> 10:31.597
What about avocado?

10:31.837 --> 10:34.157
Wouldn't the oil melt and
then get divided up?

10:34.387 --> 10:35.607
Oh, right.

10:35.807 --> 10:38.297
Hey, I prefer eating that.

10:46.647 --> 10:47.887
What's wrong, Kouhei?

10:48.197 --> 10:50.427
No, it's nothing.

10:51.767 --> 10:55.237
Well then, let's consider this the finale
for this summer vacation.

10:55.487 --> 10:57.347
Cheers!

11:02.757 --> 11:05.106
Beer and <i>takoyaki</i>
are truly the perfect match.

11:05.107 --> 11:08.407
The combination of hot
and cold is absolutely wonderful.

11:09.937 --> 11:10.827
Coming right up.

11:10.917 --> 11:12.866
This side's the true Kyoto Dashi flavor,

11:12.867 --> 11:15.276
and this side is
Gindaco-style fried <i>takoyaki</i>.

11:15.277 --> 11:16.956
Alright, approved.

11:16.957 --> 11:18.286
Give me some more.

11:18.287 --> 11:19.477
What's with the tone?

11:19.857 --> 11:20.756
Let's eat.

11:20.757 --> 11:21.906
So delicious.

11:21.907 --> 11:23.297
Ah, you guys.

11:27.467 --> 11:29.327
Why suddenly bring out the camera?

11:29.577 --> 11:31.257
I borrowed it from Chisa.

11:31.377 --> 11:33.747
To keep the memories
of this drinking party.

11:34.277 --> 11:34.846
Huh?

11:34.847 --> 11:36.886
Forgot the concept of today?

11:36.887 --> 11:39.477
Before, we asked about
everyone's regrets, remember.

11:40.217 --> 11:41.816
Oh, that?

11:41.817 --> 11:43.736
That's a bit off then.

11:43.737 --> 11:44.607
Exactly.

11:44.767 --> 11:45.237
Huh?

11:45.327 --> 11:49.567
This is definitely just recording video,
not making memories.

11:50.037 --> 11:51.007
No, no.

11:51.107 --> 11:52.937
That's not what we mean.

11:53.207 --> 11:54.677
Then what do you mean?

11:54.827 --> 11:56.287
THINGS LEFT UNDONE THIS SUMMER

11:56.387 --> 11:56.996
Huh?

11:56.997 --> 11:58.917
Something's written in the corner.

11:59.287 --> 12:02.787
MUST BE DONE IN PaB STYLE

12:05.297 --> 12:07.756
Fulfill all the remaining regrets, right?

12:07.757 --> 12:10.337
Having such thoughtful juniors
is a blessing.

12:10.747 --> 12:12.886
What's with that last line?

12:12.887 --> 12:15.517
Writing it like this is like
those scam contracts!

12:15.697 --> 12:17.727
Thank you so much, Chii-chan.

12:18.287 --> 12:19.607
Well then, right now...

12:19.717 --> 12:22.107
Let the PaB-style
cooling festival begin!

12:22.427 --> 12:23.937
- Go!
- Go!

12:24.067 --> 12:26.397
- No!
- No!

12:26.927 --> 12:29.276
So that leaves my wish.

12:29.277 --> 12:30.986
If I remember correctly,

12:30.987 --> 12:33.117
you wanted to see everyone
in <i>yukata</i>, right?

12:33.642 --> 12:34.196
Wrong.

12:34.197 --> 12:34.782
WHY DO PEOPLE LOVE YUKATA?
LOVE = YUKATA

12:35.162 --> 12:36.875
I wrote "want to see you guys
wear Yukata <i>properly</i>."

12:36.876 --> 12:37.715
TO SOLVE THIS EQUATION, THERE
IS NO OTHER BOOK BUT THIS ONE TO

12:37.716 --> 12:38.588
SOLVE THIS EQUATION, THERE IS NO
OTHER BOOK BUT THIS ONE HISTORY OF

12:38.589 --> 12:39.256
YUKATA Huh?

12:39.257 --> 12:40.274
TO SOLVE THIS EQUATION, THERE
IS NO OTHER BOOK BUT THIS ONE

12:40.487 --> 12:41.826
ORIGINALLY A GARMENT
WORN WITHOUT UNDERWEAR

12:41.827 --> 12:43.728
Um... Azusa-san...

12:43.997 --> 12:45.706
Does this mean...

12:45.707 --> 12:47.837
Exactly.

12:50.807 --> 12:52.756
Everyone take off your underwear now!

12:52.757 --> 12:53.797
- I knew it!
- I knew it!

12:54.047 --> 12:55.007
Oh my.

12:55.177 --> 12:56.676
So it has to be like that.

12:56.677 --> 12:57.637
Nanaka-san?

12:58.947 --> 13:01.136
Let's go change, Chisa-chan.

13:01.137 --> 13:02.227
Sis!

13:02.567 --> 13:04.766
- Taking off underwear's no big deal.
- Sis, wait!

13:04.767 --> 13:06.816
We actually prefer it this way.

13:06.817 --> 13:08.357
Spot on.

13:08.467 --> 13:09.936
And Iori.

13:09.937 --> 13:10.472
Yes?

13:10.907 --> 13:13.907
What you're wearing is a <i>jinbei</i>
not a <i>yukata</i>, right?

13:14.257 --> 13:16.367
Ah... I suppose so.

13:16.497 --> 13:18.697
In that case, take it all off.

13:23.447 --> 13:25.537
Feels quite cool, doesn't it, Chisa-chan?

13:27.647 --> 13:29.377
Is this acceptable?

13:29.667 --> 13:30.957
Very good.

13:31.277 --> 13:33.407
Iori, you only borrowed the sash?

13:33.517 --> 13:35.596
It's just like being naked as usual.

13:35.597 --> 13:37.847
This is even more humiliating
than being naked.

13:38.277 --> 13:41.097
You were supposed to take off
your underwear too, you know.

13:42.337 --> 13:44.767
Stripping the top is enough, spare me.

13:44.947 --> 13:46.936
Chii-chan is so cute.

13:46.937 --> 13:50.107
<i>So does that mean Azusa-san
took hers off as well?</i>

13:54.237 --> 13:55.633
<i>Could it be that this person...</i>

13:56.447 --> 13:58.237
<i>took it off since she went shopping?</i>

13:58.597 --> 14:00.537
How about you, Nanaka?

14:01.287 --> 14:01.682
WANT TO MAKE TAKOYAKI: NICE! / I HAVE
A MAKER / LET'S ADD VARIOUS STUFF

14:01.683 --> 14:04.116
Next up is the <i>takoyaki</i>.

14:04.117 --> 14:04.341
WANT TO MAKE TAKOYAKI: NICE! / I HAVE
A MAKER / LET'S ADD VARIOUS STUFF

14:04.342 --> 14:06.327
What do you mean by PaB style?

14:06.497 --> 14:08.167
Don't think too deeply about it.

14:08.297 --> 14:11.127
Just take the ingredients we bought
and cook them.

14:11.547 --> 14:12.796
INGREDIENT
TAKOYAKI BATTER

14:12.797 --> 14:14.046
EGG

14:14.047 --> 14:15.226
WATER

14:15.227 --> 14:17.596
Bullshit! That "water" is bullshit!

14:17.597 --> 14:19.638
ALCOHOL
Is that how you do PaB style?

14:19.787 --> 14:21.676
Alright, let's start cooking.

14:21.677 --> 14:24.477
Hurry up or the "water" will evaporate.

14:25.127 --> 14:26.266
Iori...

14:26.267 --> 14:27.307
and Kouhei...

14:27.507 --> 14:30.527
cooking PaB style!

14:30.957 --> 14:32.227
This time will be simple.

14:32.407 --> 14:34.967
We'll be making PaB-style<i>takoyaki</i> together.

14:35.127 --> 14:37.067
That's wonderful.

14:37.207 --> 14:38.736
TAKOYAKI BATTER- JUST ENOUGH
The method is extremely easy.

14:38.737 --> 14:40.446
EGG - JUST ENOUGH
Pour all these ingredients in.

14:40.447 --> 14:41.036
WATER - A LOT
And mix well.

14:41.037 --> 14:41.997
WATER - A LOT
Like this, right?

14:44.207 --> 14:46.786
Sir, the alcohol evaporating
into my eyes,

14:46.787 --> 14:48.496
I can't stop crying.

14:48.497 --> 14:51.957
Just imagine you're chopping onions
and try to endure it.

14:52.417 --> 14:55.627
Next, pour the mixed batter
into the <i>takoyaki</i> pan.

14:55.987 --> 15:00.006
Sir, the alcohol and the batter have
separated so I can't pour it into the pan.

15:00.007 --> 15:03.057
To prevent that,
the key is to cook very quickly.

15:03.577 --> 15:06.516
Furthermore,
since this batter is highly flammable,

15:06.517 --> 15:07.647
please be careful.

15:08.017 --> 15:09.266
If you bring a flame near it,

15:09.267 --> 15:11.776
it'll be lit aflame in
the blink of an eye like this.

15:11.777 --> 15:13.606
And this is the finished product.

15:13.607 --> 15:15.447
Wow, that's amazing.

15:19.917 --> 15:22.116
I'd rather die than eat this.

15:22.117 --> 15:24.786
There's no water so it's dry as a bone.

15:24.787 --> 15:26.907
You don't need to make such a big deal.

15:27.037 --> 15:30.087
Since it's heated by fire,
the alcohol has evaporated anyway.

15:30.927 --> 15:32.087
Hey, try some.

15:32.237 --> 15:34.307
It might turn out to be an utter delight.

15:34.547 --> 15:37.007
Chii-chan, you should try one too.

15:37.397 --> 15:39.297
Oh, <i>takoyaki</i>?

15:44.097 --> 15:47.136
Do you guys...
hold a grudge against me?

15:47.137 --> 15:48.686
No, it's a misunderstanding.

15:48.687 --> 15:50.267
It was just an accident.

15:50.517 --> 15:52.396
Is the taste really that lethal?

15:52.397 --> 15:54.846
But if no one eats it,
how will we finish it?

15:54.847 --> 15:56.277
That's true, but...

15:58.497 --> 16:00.067
Chisa, are you going to eat it?

16:00.567 --> 16:02.026
Aahh...

16:02.027 --> 16:03.007
<i>You bitch.</i>

16:04.367 --> 16:05.536
Stop it, Chisa.

16:05.537 --> 16:07.036
That won't do, let me feed you.

16:07.037 --> 16:09.456
Come on, your thoughtfulness
is annoying enough.

16:09.457 --> 16:13.287
Even if it's only in name,
I'm still your girlfriend.

16:13.927 --> 16:16.206
I should do a romantic thing
every once in a while.

16:16.207 --> 16:19.047
Please save that thoughtfulness
for another situation.

16:19.167 --> 16:21.297
So open your mouth...

16:22.127 --> 16:23.637
Stop it, really.

16:23.737 --> 16:25.137
Why did you take a picture?

16:26.267 --> 16:29.056
To blackmail you
when necessary, of course.

16:29.057 --> 16:32.237
If I get executed after this, I'm screwed.

16:32.767 --> 16:33.996
You eat it!

16:33.997 --> 16:35.066
No, you eat it!

16:35.067 --> 16:36.396
Iori, aahh...

16:36.397 --> 16:37.206
Come on now.

16:37.207 --> 16:38.696
Honestly, these guys.

16:38.697 --> 16:41.157
I told you not to argue, didn't I?

16:41.657 --> 16:43.066
But it's his fault.

16:43.067 --> 16:43.866
It's Iori.

16:43.867 --> 16:45.327
It's Chisa and Kouhei's fault!

16:45.587 --> 16:47.956
Alright, alright, at times like this...

16:47.957 --> 16:50.246
just settle it with a game like always.

16:50.247 --> 16:53.456
CONTEST DRAW LOTS: FAST DRINKING
FAST TAKOYAKI EATING / BEER CHUGGING

16:53.457 --> 16:55.056
WATER: APPROX. 96%
SNACK - TAKOYAKI: APPROX. 40%

16:55.057 --> 16:55.957
ALCOHOL - BEER: APPROX. 4.5%

16:56.397 --> 17:00.087
No matter what game we play,
it's all alcohol!

17:05.717 --> 17:06.706
FAST DRINKING CONTEST

17:06.707 --> 17:07.947
FAST TAKOYAKI EATING CONTEST
Well, well.

17:08.387 --> 17:11.267
I didn't expect them
to be so considerate of us.

17:11.447 --> 17:14.227
Say what you will,
they are quite cute in their own way.

17:14.447 --> 17:17.267
I think the juniors are always cute.

17:17.497 --> 17:17.666
THINGS LEFT UNDONE THIS SUMMER

17:17.667 --> 17:20.456
So our regrets for this summer have been
resolved. THINGS LEFT UNDONE THIS SUMMER

17:20.457 --> 17:20.706
THINGS LEFT UNDONE THIS SUMMER

17:20.707 --> 17:21.497
COMPLETE Exactly. THINGS
LEFT UNDONE THIS SUMMER

17:21.937 --> 17:24.237
Now I can finally focus on job hunting.

17:24.417 --> 17:25.337
Yeah, yeah.

17:26.207 --> 17:28.406
We still have a pile of
drawings and reports.

17:28.407 --> 17:29.997
And graduate school entrance exams.

17:30.707 --> 17:33.477
It truly was a fun and
memorable drinking party.

17:34.237 --> 17:36.637
However, for them,

17:37.327 --> 17:40.547
it might be a party that leaves them
with "memory loss sequels."

17:41.057 --> 17:42.137
Spot on.

17:49.287 --> 17:50.977
Good morning, Iori.

17:51.497 --> 17:53.937
Good morning, Nanaka-san.

17:54.727 --> 17:57.147
Last night was quite the wild party.

17:58.117 --> 17:59.276
Are you okay?

17:59.277 --> 18:00.896
Yeah, I'm doing alright.

18:00.897 --> 18:02.317
Oh, right.

18:02.707 --> 18:04.957
I already told Chisa-chan.

18:05.287 --> 18:07.407
The Dolphin shop just contacted me.

18:07.887 --> 18:10.696
Dolphin, the diving equipment shop?

18:10.697 --> 18:11.367
That's right.

18:11.867 --> 18:14.206
They just opened a new branch in Palau,

18:14.207 --> 18:16.707
but they're short-staffed
so they need people to help out.

18:17.547 --> 18:20.006
Palau? I definitely want to go.

18:20.007 --> 18:20.866
Really?

18:20.867 --> 18:23.717
It will be for about two weeks
starting next week, can you go?

18:24.497 --> 18:25.177
Yes!

18:25.367 --> 18:29.097
I was just discussing with Chisa
about wanting to go diving abroad.

18:29.927 --> 18:30.877
That's great.

18:31.247 --> 18:33.487
And what about Kouhei-kun?

18:33.717 --> 18:35.687
If I invite Kouhei for a part-time job...

18:36.547 --> 18:37.936
<i>Abroad?</i>

18:37.937 --> 18:38.646
<i>No way.</i>

18:38.647 --> 18:41.187
<i>How would I watch anime
when it broadcasts then?</i>

18:42.847 --> 18:45.147
Let me talk to Kouhei myself.

18:45.877 --> 18:46.487
Is that so?

18:46.677 --> 18:48.117
Then I'll leave it to you.

18:48.407 --> 18:50.027
I'll send the message later.

18:50.127 --> 18:52.107
Yes, take care.

18:59.067 --> 18:59.737
Oh.

19:00.027 --> 19:01.207
Hey.

19:03.037 --> 19:05.427
Last night was quite the wild party.

19:05.907 --> 19:06.797
Indeed.

19:07.057 --> 19:07.977
Are you okay?

19:08.207 --> 19:09.337
I'm doing alright.

19:09.747 --> 19:11.056
By the way, Kouhei.

19:11.057 --> 19:12.097
What is it?

19:12.217 --> 19:13.386
Nanaka-san said...

19:13.387 --> 19:17.557
the new branch of Dolphin is short-staffed
and needs help.

19:18.027 --> 19:19.186
Want a part-time job?

19:19.187 --> 19:20.687
Two weeks, starting next week.

19:21.197 --> 19:22.476
That's very sudden.

19:22.477 --> 19:24.107
And for two whole weeks?

19:24.707 --> 19:27.777
But you need some money to take
the Advance license exam, right?

19:28.027 --> 19:29.427
True, but...

19:29.727 --> 19:31.656
You get practical diving experience,

19:31.657 --> 19:33.997
and you might get to buy
equipment at a discount.

19:34.567 --> 19:37.247
Hearing that makes it sound
quite tempting.

19:37.367 --> 19:40.207
So you're joining too?

19:40.737 --> 19:42.447
I guess so.

19:42.857 --> 19:46.006
But let me warn you,
I won't accept night shifts.

19:46.007 --> 19:48.377
This summer's anime
is reaching its climax.

19:48.627 --> 19:52.387
I have to watch my favorite shows live
when they are broadcasting.

19:52.617 --> 19:54.567
CONFIRMED! KOUHEI WILL ALSO GO!!
You can do whatever you want.

19:55.147 --> 19:56.407
By the way, Kouhei.

19:56.587 --> 19:59.167
Where did you go for your field trip
in high school?

19:59.737 --> 20:01.186
Australia,

20:01.187 --> 20:02.397
why do you ask?

20:02.787 --> 20:04.526
I see, I see.

20:04.527 --> 20:06.026
What's with that weird smile?

20:06.027 --> 20:07.207
No, it's nothing.

20:07.357 --> 20:10.447
So when and where is this job?

20:10.587 --> 20:13.616
9 AM next Monday,
at Narita Airport.

20:13.617 --> 20:15.987
Okay, 9 AM at Narita.

20:16.657 --> 20:17.057
Huh?

20:17.607 --> 20:18.516
Wait a minute.

20:18.517 --> 20:19.826
Is there a problem?

20:19.827 --> 20:23.287
That new branch...
is at Narita Airport, right?

20:24.337 --> 20:25.417
Of course it is.

20:25.547 --> 20:27.466
But remember to bring your passport.

20:27.467 --> 20:29.507
Getting me to go abroad, you bastard!?

20:30.027 --> 20:33.297
NANAKA KOTEGAWA
Sorry, I already texted her that we're in.

20:33.627 --> 20:35.057
What? But...

20:35.177 --> 20:37.476
I need time to prepare as well.

20:37.477 --> 20:38.707
Don't worry.

20:38.827 --> 20:41.777
Clothes, food, and lodging are all
taken care of by them.

20:42.047 --> 20:45.977
I also just confirmed that
your passport is still valid.

20:47.437 --> 20:51.066
In short, just set your anime to record
and let's go have fun together.

20:51.067 --> 20:51.987
No!

20:52.187 --> 20:55.866
My precious live viewing time!

20:55.867 --> 20:57.947
KITAHARA INN

20:59.957 --> 21:01.457
IORI

21:01.707 --> 21:03.127
It's big brother.

21:06.867 --> 21:08.837
Hello, Kitahara speaking.

21:08.977 --> 21:10.487
Oh, Shiori?

21:10.837 --> 21:12.757
What's up?

21:12.877 --> 21:14.757
Nothing much.

21:14.957 --> 21:17.177
Are you calling about your allowance?

21:17.327 --> 21:20.226
True, this month's money
hasn't hit my account yet.

21:20.227 --> 21:21.597
But that's not it.

21:22.017 --> 21:25.186
So you're planning to visit home?

21:25.187 --> 21:26.834
Sorry, but I have a favor to ask.

21:28.007 --> 21:30.757
I want you to find and send
my passport to me right now.

21:30.887 --> 21:32.907
Your passport?

21:33.047 --> 21:35.117
Why do you need it all of a sudden?

21:35.327 --> 21:36.866
It's a bit sudden, but...

21:36.867 --> 21:40.327
I've decided to spend the rest
of my summer vacation abroad.

21:41.187 --> 21:41.487
Tch.

21:42.327 --> 21:43.017
Huh?

21:48.007 --> 21:50.507
For some reason, she refuses to send it.

21:50.767 --> 21:51.706
Oh boy.

21:51.707 --> 21:54.676
Your first summer away from home
and you don't visit even once,

21:54.677 --> 21:56.047
you reap what you sow.

21:56.557 --> 21:59.287
So the only way
is to go home and get it yourself?

22:01.287 --> 22:02.707
That's the only way.

22:02.837 --> 22:04.407
Is there a problem?

22:04.587 --> 22:06.517
Of course there is.

22:07.047 --> 22:09.227
I sense bad vibes
coming from right over there.

22:10.717 --> 22:13.806
TOUR TO VISIT
BIOLOGICAL SISTER SHIORI

22:13.807 --> 22:14.977
SISCON BROTHER

22:19.627 --> 22:21.247
<i>3... 2... 1... Go!</i>

22:30.797 --> 22:33.546
<i>A sweet little love story!?</i>

22:33.547 --> 22:36.336
<i>Asymmetrical reflection in the mirror</i>

22:36.337 --> 22:37.926
<i>A shattered, crunchy heart</i>

22:37.927 --> 22:40.007
<i>Oh oh, stumbling around</i>

22:40.557 --> 22:42.976
<i>Oh oh, just acting on instinct</i>

22:42.977 --> 22:46.936
<i>Diving deep into my subconscious</i>

22:46.937 --> 22:48.726
<i>Tumbling and falling down</i>

22:48.727 --> 22:51.276
<i>A limit-breaking paradise</i>

22:51.277 --> 22:52.526
<i>Viva, cheers</i>

22:52.527 --> 22:53.986
<i>Everyone, cheers</i>

22:53.987 --> 22:56.066
<i>We're in trouble, we're in trouble</i>

22:56.067 --> 22:56.776
<i>Big trouble</i>

22:56.777 --> 22:58.776
<i>We're in trouble, we're in trouble</i>

22:58.777 --> 22:59.576
<i>Wa wa wa</i>

22:59.577 --> 23:01.536
<i>We're in trouble, we're in trouble</i>

23:01.537 --> 23:02.246
<i>Wa wa wa wa</i>

23:02.247 --> 23:04.206
<i>Let's go, everybody</i>

23:04.207 --> 23:07.666
<i>Dramatic just like a rainbow</i>

23:07.667 --> 23:10.706
<i>Your troubled smile
is absolutely priceless</i>

23:10.707 --> 23:15.966
<i>Total chaos
getting kissed by an octopus</i>

23:15.967 --> 23:18.716
<i>A mermaid washed up on the shore</i>

23:18.717 --> 23:21.676
<i>Darling drowned down
in the Dragon Palace</i>

23:21.677 --> 23:26.936
<i>The treasure box is just full of alcohol</i>

23:26.937 --> 23:29.646
<i>The ultimate license of our youth</i>

23:29.647 --> 23:32.646
<i>Find the treasure and checkmate</i>

23:32.647 --> 23:37.856
<i>An angel who overslept
from swimming too much</i>

23:37.857 --> 23:39.316
<i>Let's go, everybody</i>

23:39.317 --> 23:40.696
<i>Viva, cheers</i>

23:40.697 --> 23:42.026
<i>Oh yeah</i>

23:42.027 --> 23:43.697
<i>Viva, cheers</i>

23:44.947 --> 23:49.957
NEXT EPISODE: GOING HOME
